INSERT INTO "opportunity" VALUES(30,1,1,1,1,21,25,NULL,NULL,2,NULL,'CONFIRMED','2026-07-31',NULL,NULL,'Python AI Engineer','6-months','Python Developer with AI experience Looking for 6-8 years of overall Python development experience with at least 1 year of AI experience IV will consist of technologies used, projects completed with relevant technologies, team fit & personality • Replacing manual human-approval process where information is gathered and decisions are made against proposals for new products or expansion into new markets: involves regulations, policies, laws, regional rules, and legal ramifications. • Want to use AI support to summarize requirements, assess risk, and help build rubrics/scoring models for decision-making. • Will support work spanning risk, compliance, legal, finance, and technology review areas. • Anything produced by the agent will still be reviewed by a person, and then a sign-off owner in each area will either approve or reject the findings. MUST HAVES: • Strong Python proficiency is required. • Experience with GenAI, agentic AI frameworks, MCP-enabled application components, and familiarity with how the AI lifecycle works: they don’t need to have built many agents from scratch, but they should have touched GenAI work and understand how the AI lifecycle can be used to replace manual work. • Must have strong knowledge of REST APIs and microservices, since those are needed to expose tools through MCP servers. • Postgres is a must. Oracle is good to have. Other relational databases are acceptable • PL/SQL nuances can be learned fairly quickly. CI/CD pipelines are already built. • Would like experience building or using agents, or tools for MCP servers and agentic workflows. • Framework experience such as LangChain or LangGraph is acceptable, but Team uses Google ADK. • Should understand concepts like RAG databases and vector embeddings. • Financial services preferred, but can come from other highly regulated industries like healthcare. Small shops are also OK – they can teach the business rules Job Description This is a development position within the Technology organization responsible for building and supporting modern software solutions leveraging Python, microservices, APIs, event-driven architectures, and emerging AI technologies. The role will contribute to the development of Agentic AI solutions, MCP integrations, and distributed application platforms. The successful candidate will work closely with senior engineers, architects, and business partners to deliver scalable and secure applications while adhering to established engineering and governance standards. Responsibilities As a Software Engineer, you will: Design, develop, test, and support Python-based applications and services. Build and maintain REST APIs, microservices, and event-driven integrations. Contribute to development of Agentic AI workflows and MCP-enabled application components. Implement integrations between AI models, enterprise systems, and business applications. Develop reusable services and components following enterprise engineering standards. Participate in the full software development lifecycle, including design, coding, testing, deployment, and support. Implement monitoring, logging, and operational controls to ensure service reliability. Contribute to automation, CI/CD pipelines, and testing frameworks. Work with messaging and event-streaming technologies to support asynchronous processing. Collaborate with business and technology teams to analyze requirements and develop technical solutions. Support issue resolution, performance tuning, and application enhancements. Document technical designs, implementation details, and operational procedures. Follow established security, governance, and risk management standards. Qualifications Bachelor''s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Information Systems, or related STEM field. 2–5 years of experience developing applications using Python. Experience with RESTful APIs and microservices development. Familiarity with event-driven architecture and messaging platforms. Experience with FastAPI, Flask, or similar Python frameworks. Knowledge of SQL and database technologies. Familiarity with source control, CI/CD pipelines, and automated testing. Experience working in Linux environments. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively within cross-functional teams. Preferred Skills Exposure to Agentic AI frameworks, MCP, LLMs, and GenAI solutions. Familiarity with Kafka, MQ, or event-streaming platforms. Experience with cloud platforms and container technologies. Banking, risk management, or financial services experience. Understanding of distributed systems, observability, and platform monitoring. Education Bachelor''s degree/University degree or equivalent experience in a STEM-related field. Advanced degree preferred.','-','On-Site','7/31/2026|motion recruitment|python ai engineer|citi group','csv','C2C','Hourly',85.0,85.0,'USD',NULL,'Onsite','Irving','Texas','2026-09-01 20:01:25.112295','2026-09-02 16:01:37.680806');
